            <ArticleTitle>[Teenagers' drawings in transcultural consultations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1259-4792(16)30131-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.spp.2016.11.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The place of teenagers' drawings has been studied as part of a transcultural consultation, based on the creativity of the children of migrants. When speaking is difficult, drawings enable teenagers to show another dimension of their internal world. Aravin, a young Tamil boy, who lacked the necessary words, was able to express all the complexity of his thoughts through his drawings, finally being able to formulate in the group the difficult situations which he was drawing.</AbstractText>
